    {
      "id": "library/10665-339745/blocks/prose-sec-003",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Objectives",
      "pageStart": 14,
      "pageEnd": 15,
      "target": "../sections/sec-003-objectives.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "This DAK focuses on antenatal care (ANC) and aims to provide a common language across various audiences – maternal health and other programme \nmanagers, software developers, and implementers of digital systems – to ensure a common understanding of the appropriate health information content \nwithin the ANC health programme area, as a mechanism to catalyse the effective use of these digital systems. The key objectives of this DAK are:\n\t»\nto ensure adherence to WHO clinical, public health and data use guidelines, and facilitate consistency of the health content that is used to inform \nthe develop",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Sets out the objectives of the antenatal care digital adaptation kit: providing a shared language for programme managers, developers and implementers and ensuring digital tracking and decision-support systems follow WHO guidance. It notes links to other kits, including a forthcoming one on self-care.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/10665-339745/blocks/prose-sec-004",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Components of a digital adaptation kit",
      "pageStart": 15,
      "pageEnd": 19,
      "target": "../sections/sec-004-components-of-a-digital-adaptation-kit.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "The DAK comprises eight interlinked components: (1) health interventions and associated recommendations; (2) generic personas; (3) user scenarios; \n(4) generic business processes and workflows; (5) core data elements; (6) decision-support logic; (7) indicators and reporting requirements; and (8) high-\nlevel functional and non-functional requirements. Table 1 provides an overview of each of the contributing components of the DAK, which this document \nelaborates. All information within the adaptation kit represents a generic starting point, which can then be adapted according to the specific con",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Describes the eight interlinked components of the digital adaptation kit, from health interventions and recommendations, personas and user scenarios to workflows, core data elements, decision-support logic, indicators and functional requirements. A table explains the purpose, outputs and adaptation needed for each component. It also notes the kit builds on PATH's work on maternal health information system requirements and explains naming conventions for requirement identifiers.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/10665-339745/blocks/prose-sec-005",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "How to use this digital adaptation kit",
      "pageStart": 19,
      "pageEnd": 22,
      "target": "../sections/sec-005-how-to-use-this-digital-adaptation-kit.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Target audience\nThe primary target audience for this DAK is health programme managers within the ministry of health (MOH), who will be working with their digital or \nhealth information systems counterparts in determining the health content requirements for an ANC DTDS system. The health programme manager is \nresponsible for overseeing and monitoring the implementation of the clinical practices and policies for the health programme area, in this case ANC. \nThe DAK also equips individuals responsible for translating health-system processes and guidance documents for use within digital systems wi",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "Identifies the main audience as ministry of health programme managers working with digital and information system teams, along with business analysts who translate guidance into system requirements. It describes the modular design linked to other health areas and scenarios for use, such as checking existing systems against WHO content or building a new point-of-care client record. It also explains terminology such as the use of \"client\" and \"woman\".",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "library/10665-339745/blocks/prose-sec-006",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "Linkages to the broader digital health ecosystem",
      "pageStart": 22,
      "pageEnd": 95,
      "target": "../sections/sec-006-linkages-to-the-broader-digital-health-ecosystem.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Digital adaptation kits within the broader digital \nhealth ecosystem\nFIG. 3\nWHO Core \nindicator \nsets\nGlobal \ndigital \nhealth \nindex\nWHO Digital \nhealth atlas\nDigital \nhealth \ninvestment \nreview tool\nHIS Stages of  \ncontinuous \nimprovement\n+\t Conduct an inventory of existing or previously used \nsoftware applications, ICT systems and other tools to better \nunderstand the requirements for reuse and interoperability\n+\t Develop a national digital health strategy outlining \noverarching needs, desired activities and outcomes\n+\t Define a vision for how the health system will be \nstrengthened through",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "A very long section covering most of the antenatal care digital adaptation kit, opening with how such kits fit into the wider digital health ecosystem and a seven-phase planning process. It lists the antenatal care interventions drawn from WHO's universal health coverage compendium and the WHO guidelines the kit reflects, including those on antenatal care, tuberculosis screening, HIV, malaria and syphilis. Its later parts set out the kit's components, such as personas, workflows, data elements, decision logic and indicators. It ends with annex guidance on filling in a data dictionary, including required fields, skip logic, links to aggregate indicators and concept mappings to ICD-11 or SNOMED.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
      }
